es behavior when a `type: \"result\"` envelope exists, and only Claude Code emits one. The Codex wrapper passes its `-o` final-message file as the last output, so `extract_findings` already read that file first, and with no result envelope it still uses the last object. Codex users get no behavior change, so the entry overstates what was fixed. This fragment also leaves out the error-result behavior the change adds: an `is_error` result now fails with \"reviewer CLI reported an error result\" instead of falling back to an earlier object.","fix_commit":"10078c76ca18ab55db7e8f73e6777309193c09bd","id":"F002","line":1,"path":"docs/CHANGELOG.d/reviewer-trailing-stream-events.fixed.md","response_note":null,"severity":"low","stage":"review","status":"fixed","suggestion":"Limit the entry to the Claude wrapper, and add that a Claude result envelope marked `is_error` now fails the review with its subtype instead of using an earlier findings object.","title":"Changelog fragment says the fix also covers the Codex wrapper, which it does not change","unit":"U0002"}],"fingerprint":{"base_tree_sha":"287498923ff6fe4e8d3a0349c62cc05064ed0215","config_sha256":"ac4e49f56b3ae75162d42ec2ca923d2a7c1e5c61e299c18997aae9839b85185c","configuration_supported":true,"diff_sha256":"cb7d965ebdc1f15a5be44b0da2aa9a36adb0f27ef5e93b2126a6ae152ccc7c2b","excluded_files":[],"executor":"command","grounding_sha256":"5ca18ae496422a3233e5cf6aaefa01a068b35de01092a9cade7ce8e6097ab136","head_tree_sha":"5409af1d8c613aff28be71eb20eac806d777887d","intent_sha256":"1c21ee3d820f331d64c248bdf8ea1bc4d1594fc22c79b8117025c86c49e52898","version":2},"finished_at":"2026-10-30T08:07:44Z","head_sha":"10078c76ca18ab55db7e8f73e6777309193c09bd","result":{"command":"env AP_REVIEWER_MODEL=claude-opus-5-5 AP_REVIEWER_EFFORT=low python3 -B docs/examples/reviewers/claude_review.py","coverage":{"cited_units":[],"clean_units":["U0001","U0002","U0003","U0004","U0005"],"excluded_files":[],"grounding_sha256":"5ca18ae496422a3233e5cf6aaefa0